omx-contract (3.20.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * omx-contract 3.20.0: a domain document is <domain>/<last segment>.json
  * omx-contract 3.20.0: the domain document, its C loader, and the scan,
    machine and qualification words out
  * ownership: contract.catalog.invalid is omx-contract's own code
  * consumer-move: step 6 rewrapped to the line width
  * consumer-move: a repository without a Makefile calls the installer from
    its packaging
  * consumer-move: the worked example is plugin-hostd#167
  * consumer-move: fmt is a step of a move
  * %{omx_contract_domain_dir}: the RPM macro of the domain directory
  * Test the RPM macro of the domain directory, before it exists
  * style: reformat the domain fixtures with the new fmt rule
  * fix: fmt formats a domain document by the one rule
  * consumer-move: two paragraphs rewrapped to the line width
  * consumer-move: a domain ships in a <pkg>-contract subpackage, with its
    macro
  * test: fmt formats a domain document by the one rule (red)
  * consumer-move: no note about a loader that was never released
  * consumer-move: words passed on as strings need no mark; description is
    optional
  * consumer-move: the worked example is plugin-hostd#165; fmt names its issue
  * consumer-move: fmt is not part of a move; arm 5 may be n/a; read and
    install ship together
  * consumer-move: step 6 names the installer PR and its refusals
  * Install a domain with install-contract-dir.sh --domain
  * Test install-contract-dir.sh --domain, before the mode exists
  * consumer-move: the front lines a recipe index reads
  * The fuzz harness reads a word whose description is NULL
  * Red: the fuzz corpus holds a word without a description
  * Format the merged codes and label the catalog sentences lane-draft
  * fix: the C loader accepts a word with no description
  * test: the C loader must open a word with no description
  * consumer-move: a domain installs with the installer's domain mode; an
    installed-tree arm
  * docs/consumer-move.md: the recipe of one consumer move onto a domain
  * Require info.x-stability in the C domain loader
  * Test the C domain loader's info.x-stability
  * codes: contract.item.prefix is appended to CONTRACT_CODES, not inserted
  * The domain schema requires info.x-stability and allows nested x-from refs
  * Red: the domain schema requires info.x-stability, allows nested x-from
    refs, names the nested path
  * An x-from $ref may name a nested domain
  * The reader requires info.x-stability, experimental or stable
  * Red: a domain document must carry info.x-stability, experimental or stable
  * The domain document has a schema: schema/domain.schema.json, exported,
    typed, installed
  * Red: the domain document has a schema, shipped beside the data schema
  * catalogs: the five contract.item.prefix entries are lane-draft machine
    text
  * The C loader refuses a bad catalog as contract.catalog.invalid
  * contract.catalog.invalid: a bad catalog of a domain has its own code (red)
  * Close the spec gaps of the C domain loader
  * Test the C domain loader's spec gaps, red: x-code place, duplicate keys,
    $ref, ranges, catalogs, owner
  * A path the loader cannot hold is contract.manifest.invalid, not
    contract.dir.absent
  * Test: a path the loader cannot hold is refused as an unusable input, by
    code
  * Fix the C domain loader's memory-safety bugs
  * Test the C domain loader's memory safety, red: fuzz target, corpus,
    hostile-directory tests
  * debian: libomx-domain0 symbols file, so consumers get a version floor
  * check-abi counts every exported symbol, data as well as functions
  * Tests: check-abi must catch an exported data symbol, and the package must
    give consumers a floor
  * The qualification domain items carry the domain prefix
  * descriptor check: a choiceUnits key must name a control and a choice
    control
  * The prefix check takes the domain from the one document-path rule of the
    reader
  * Red: the prefix check takes the domain from the document path the reader
    uses
  * The ownership lists follow the qualification domain out
  * The ownership lists follow the machine domain out
  * The ownership lists follow the scan domain out
  * A domain renders its codes header only, and its item names carry the
    domain prefix
  * docs: a domain's file path and its $id stated apart
  * Red: a domain renders only its codes header, and its item names carry the
    domain prefix
  * omx_domain: a domain name is a slash-separated path, the file is named by
    its last segment
  * test: nested domain names open, and an invalid path is refused by name,
    red against the flat loader
  * docs: a domain name is a slash-separated path; omx_domain_text is NULL
    for a word with no x-text
  * schema: x-omx-schema-version 3.20.0 for the $id change
  * schema ids: omx-contract.schema.json at /v3/, the vocabulary at its major
  * schema-ids: every $id names the major version only
  * Spec: OMX_<ITEM>_<WORD>, every item name starts with its domain
  * Spec: a domain renders its codes header only, marked x-c-codes
  * docs: BUILDING lists the C loader's packages
  * release and tests: the loader's packages are built, listed and held to
